1
00:00:31,615 --> 00:00:34,617
<i>There are some things one should wish for...</i>

2
00:00:35,452 --> 00:00:37,778
<i>and some you should leave alone.</i>

3
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:44,959
<i>That's what my little brother, Frankie, told me.</i>

4
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:52,624
<i>He said I only had three wishes.</i>

5
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:57,174
<i>I looked him in the eyes.</i>

6
00:00:58,683 --> 00:01:00,677
<i>I don't know why I believed him.</i>

7
00:01:38,974 --> 00:01:43,186
- Remember that we are on holiday.
- Stop it, Christy.

8
00:01:44,354 --> 00:01:47,641
<i>Those with US passports
should use the files on the left.</i>

9
00:01:54,906 --> 00:01:58,490
- Can I see the passports?
- We are on vacation!

10
00:01:59,369 --> 00:02:02,988
- Are you, my girl?
- Yes. And dad won't be working.

11
00:02:16,928 --> 00:02:18,922
What are you going to do in the US?

12
00:02:19,014 --> 00:02:20,046
We are on vacation.

13
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:22,846
- How long have you been in Canada?
- Visiting.

14
00:02:22,934 --> 00:02:24,595
<i>When I listened to mother and father...</i>

15
00:02:24,686 --> 00:02:26,727
We bought the car in Canada.

16
00:02:26,813 --> 00:02:30,266
<i>... I was afraid we weren't allowed to come
over the border.</i>

17
00:02:30,901 --> 00:02:35,694
<i>If I didn't talk to Frankie,
how then would we enter the United States?</i>

18
00:02:37,949 --> 00:02:41,070
<i>“Please, Frankie.</i>

19
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:43,495
<i>“Help us,” I said.</i>

20
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:46,154
- How many children do you have?
- Three.

21
00:02:46,249 --> 00:02:47,365
Two.

22
00:02:49,669 --> 00:02:50,785
Two.

23
00:02:51,755 --> 00:02:55,041
- It says three here.
- We've lost one.

24
00:03:06,269 --> 00:03:09,022
- What is your name, my girl?
- Ariel.

25
00:03:11,483 --> 00:03:13,144
What is your name?

26
00:03:15,529 --> 00:03:17,072
Her name is Christy.

27
00:03:17,781 --> 00:03:20,487
- How old are you, Christy?
- She is 10.

28
00:03:25,747 --> 00:03:28,500
- Welcome to the USA.
- Thank you very much.

29
00:03:37,759 --> 00:03:40,382
<i>Thus I had used up
the first wish.</i>

30
00:03:41,346 --> 00:03:43,423
<i>But I had two left.</i>

31
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:52,482
<i>We could hear Manhattan before we saw it.</i>

32
00:03:52,566 --> 00:03:55,852
<i>Thousands of foreign voices everywhere.</i>

33
00:03:59,406 --> 00:04:01,530
<i>You probably don't believe this...</i>

34
00:04:01,616 --> 00:04:04,488
<i>but we had to go under the water
to get to town.</i>

35
00:04:04,578 --> 00:04:07,864
<i>No, it's true.
It was a proper alien.</i>

36
00:04:08,290 --> 00:04:10,912
<i>We lost touch with everything.</i>

37
00:04:11,293 --> 00:04:14,045
<i>It was like being on another planet.</i>

38
00:04:32,647 --> 00:04:35,898
<i>...classics from the 60s, 70s, 80s and 90s...</i>

39
00:05:54,855 --> 00:05:58,141
<i>We searched all over Manhattan
looking for a place to live...</i>

40
00:05:58,441 --> 00:06:02,855
<i>before we finally found the house
with the man screaming.</i>

41
00:06:06,616 --> 00:06:09,819
What are you doing with that camera, girl?

42
00:06:11,079 --> 00:06:12,788
- Are you police?
- What?

43
00:06:12,873 --> 00:06:14,154
Watch your fingers.

44
00:06:14,583 --> 00:06:17,288
- Are you police?
- No, we're Irish.

45
00:06:17,669 --> 00:06:20,161
- All Irish are police.
- Not us.

46
00:06:20,338 --> 00:06:22,665
Shall we live here now?

47
00:06:22,799 --> 00:06:25,754
- Are you going to live here in this block?
- Yes.

48
00:06:27,179 --> 00:06:31,047
Right. Keep an eye on the car.
Papo will look after you now.

49
00:06:31,349 --> 00:06:34,766
Come in.
Welcome to your new manor.

50
00:06:39,733 --> 00:06:41,014
Come on again.

51
00:06:42,152 --> 00:06:44,145
Look, an elevator!

52
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:49,446
It hasn't worked in ages. Come on.

53
00:07:01,671 --> 00:07:03,630
- Shall we live here now?
- Yes.

54
00:07:03,715 --> 00:07:06,088
- Why?
- Nobody else wants us.

55
00:07:06,218 --> 00:07:09,255
- Why not?
- They don't want children in Manhattan.

56
00:07:09,346 --> 00:07:12,763
- Why not?
- Why do you think it's called "Mann"hattan?

57
00:07:15,185 --> 00:07:16,384
STAY AWAY

58
00:07:18,522 --> 00:07:20,895
Papo, don't come any closer.

59
00:07:20,982 --> 00:07:24,186
Relax, Tony. It's just me.

60
00:07:24,277 --> 00:07:26,947
I know that.
Go back down to your apartment.

61
00:07:27,030 --> 00:07:30,365
I am sober.
I'll show them the empty apartment.

62
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:32,907
- Don't talk about, Papo.
- Right.

63
00:07:32,994 --> 00:07:35,996
Right, Papo. We'll take over from here.

64
00:07:41,378 --> 00:07:44,914
- Why is he screaming?
- Maybe he sees ghosts.

65
00:07:45,632 --> 00:07:47,673
Is this house haunted?

66
00:07:56,393 --> 00:07:58,517
- It's like Fort Knox.
- Cool.

67
00:07:58,603 --> 00:08:00,763
- Where did you learn that?
- What then?

68
00:08:00,856 --> 00:08:03,145
- "Cool".
- I just heard that.

69
00:08:03,233 --> 00:08:06,151
You are already an American. Disgusting.

70
00:08:07,112 --> 00:08:10,030
- First man in, Christy.
- How big it is!

71
00:08:10,115 --> 00:08:12,192
Yes. It is huge.

72
00:08:12,284 --> 00:08:14,194
- This is my room.
- It's big.

73
00:08:14,286 --> 00:08:16,493
- This is my room.
- I want the top bunk.

74
00:08:16,580 --> 00:08:20,032
Look, Dad. There is a bathtub in the middle of the room.

75
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:26,623
There are pigeons! Look here, Ariel.

76
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:30,459
- It's a bit of a mess.
- It will be good when we get it refurbished.

77
00:08:31,803 --> 00:08:33,761
It's going to cost, Sarah.

78
00:08:37,392 --> 00:08:40,014
How are we going to pay for this?

79
00:08:40,729 --> 00:08:42,521
We are selling the car.

80
00:08:45,901 --> 00:08:47,693
- Are you okay?
- Yes.

81
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:49,273
- Sure?
- Yes, then.

82
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:50,644
Absolutely sure?

83
00:08:54,784 --> 00:08:56,778
- Dad?
- What is it?

84
00:08:57,078 --> 00:08:59,119
Can we keep the pigeons?

85
00:09:01,249 --> 00:09:03,539
Dad, can we keep the pigeons?

86
00:09:07,631 --> 00:09:09,920
No, we have to let them out.

87
00:09:22,479 --> 00:09:25,979
<i>It seemed like all our problems
flew his way.</i>

88
00:09:33,323 --> 00:09:36,942
- Can I help, dad?
- Ask mom.

89
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:41,242
- Can I help, mom?
- Can't you skate?

90
00:09:41,331 --> 00:09:43,905
<i>I'm skipping this here.</i>

91
00:09:58,640 --> 00:10:01,891
<i>Ariel got to know everyone in the neighborhood.</i>

92
00:10:09,943 --> 00:10:12,150
<i>Mum didn't get a job as a teacher.</i>

93
00:10:12,237 --> 00:10:16,699
<i>So she took a job at the ice cream parlor
so dad could audition.</i>

94
00:10:22,122 --> 00:10:24,365
I like the role.

95
00:10:24,791 --> 00:10:26,619
I'm glad I was able to come again.

96
00:10:26,710 --> 00:10:29,665
I just want to say that I appreciate it.

97
00:10:31,548 --> 00:10:33,506
Has he considered the role of Vinny?

98
00:10:33,592 --> 00:10:36,629
The New York type? He is a bit of a stereotype.

99
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:39,212
But if you want him, that's fine.

100
00:10:40,599 --> 00:10:42,758
Can you speak with a London accent?

101
00:10:43,810 --> 00:10:46,018
Are you kidding? He only has two lines.

102
00:10:46,104 --> 00:10:49,391
Shall I come up and beat you up?

103
00:10:52,194 --> 00:10:54,068
- Do you like him?
- Yes.

104
00:10:54,154 --> 00:10:57,109
But acting is about
more than accents.

105
00:10:57,782 --> 00:11:01,532
I would love to give you a role.
But you must give me much more.

106
00:11:01,620 --> 00:11:03,329
Don't you understand?

107
00:11:03,413 --> 00:11:07,032
Get it out of your head.
It comes from here and from here.

108
00:11:07,375 --> 00:11:09,499
Just give me one more chance.

109
00:11:10,086 --> 00:11:12,460
<i>But he didn't get any more chances.</i>

110
00:11:12,547 --> 00:11:16,546
<i>Then summer came.
And with it came the heat.</i>

111
00:11:19,513 --> 00:11:22,468
<i>And a new word: humidity.</i>

112
00:11:25,519 --> 00:11:28,093
- Dad, it still doesn't work.
- Wait.

113
00:11:34,194 --> 00:11:35,689
It's too hot.

114
00:11:39,658 --> 00:11:43,407
- It still doesn't come out of the holes.
- Just wait.

115
00:11:46,373 --> 00:11:48,912
Wait.

116
00:11:49,668 --> 00:11:51,745
It's coming.

117
00:11:56,591 --> 00:11:58,087
It works.

118
00:12:02,305 --> 00:12:05,722
- Good, Dad. It's deliciously cold.
- I'm so happy for you.

119
00:12:08,937 --> 00:12:11,476
Ariel, dad is going to an audition.

120
00:12:11,773 --> 00:12:13,185
- Dad!
- Yes?

121
00:12:14,818 --> 00:12:17,820
- What are you doing?
- I read scripts.

122
00:12:18,405 --> 00:12:21,027
- Why that?
- I learn my lines.

123
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:29,036
Can we stay here all day, dad?

124
00:12:33,170 --> 00:12:35,875
- Dad, it's fine in America.
- So nice.

125
00:12:37,257 --> 00:12:38,669
- Dad?
- Yes?

126
00:12:39,176 --> 00:12:40,457
Nothing.

127
00:12:59,279 --> 00:13:01,273
What are we doing?

128
00:13:12,417 --> 00:13:14,210
Dad, Ariel is upset.

129
00:13:14,836 --> 00:13:18,502
- She has been in the bath for too long.
- What's the matter?

130
00:13:18,590 --> 00:13:20,299
- The feet are wrinkled.
- What?

131
00:13:20,383 --> 00:13:21,879
They are like prunes.

132
00:13:21,968 --> 00:13:24,425
You big mine. where is mom?

133
00:13:34,648 --> 00:13:36,143
are you ok

134
00:13:40,195 --> 00:13:41,690
It's too hot.

135
00:13:45,534 --> 00:13:49,947
Dad, how are you going to get the air conditioner
up and down from the pavement?

136
00:13:52,082 --> 00:13:54,206
Dad, how are you going to…

137
00:13:57,170 --> 00:13:58,452
Come on!

138
00:14:02,509 --> 00:14:04,467
Dad, they're shooting you.

139
00:14:14,062 --> 00:14:15,854
- Watch out, dad!
- Shit!

140
00:14:20,944 --> 00:14:22,523
Look, it's dad.

141
00:14:27,284 --> 00:14:30,701
- You're on drugs, Papo.
- No.

142
00:14:30,912 --> 00:14:32,491
Don't Go...

143
00:14:35,167 --> 00:14:37,789
Can I have some of what he has taken?

144
00:14:38,295 --> 00:14:40,004
Crazy ire!

145
00:15:06,615 --> 00:15:08,608
Christy, open the door!

146
00:15:08,783 --> 00:15:12,533
Mom, Dad has an air conditioner!

147
00:15:12,621 --> 00:15:14,698
He's coming!

148
00:15:17,751 --> 00:15:20,872
- Move! Now!
- You're having a heart attack.

149
00:15:21,838 --> 00:15:24,626
- Open the window!
- Open the window, mom!

150
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:18,019
What is wrong?

151
00:16:20,105 --> 00:16:21,565
Wrong plug.

152
00:16:22,023 --> 00:16:23,649
40°! HEAT WAVE

153
00:16:26,194 --> 00:16:27,606
25 cents too little.

154
00:16:27,696 --> 00:16:30,899
It doesn't hold.
I have to earn a living. $1.99.

155
00:16:31,575 --> 00:16:33,864
You will get them tomorrow.

156
00:16:34,494 --> 00:16:37,662
- Aren't you from the drug block?
- So what?

157
00:16:38,290 --> 00:16:39,785
Look there.

158
00:16:40,876 --> 00:16:43,628
I was holding the knife of a drug addict.

159
00:16:43,712 --> 00:16:46,334
I got 25 stitches. He got probation.

160
00:16:50,635 --> 00:16:53,009
Do I look like a drug addict?

161
00:16:56,016 --> 00:16:57,808
$1.99.

162
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:25,417
- What are you doing?
- We get 5 cents for each of them.

163
00:17:26,630 --> 00:17:31,091
- Where is the $100 I gave you?
- At the bank, as you requested.

164
00:17:49,903 --> 00:17:51,398
And 25 cents.

165
00:17:54,991 --> 00:17:58,657
And $2. Mr. American Dream.

166
00:17:59,079 --> 00:18:00,574
And one plug.

167
00:18:02,582 --> 00:18:04,077
And 1 cent.

168
00:18:09,381 --> 00:18:12,299
Take it easy, Dad. Mom is breathing fine.

169
00:18:12,384 --> 00:18:13,796
Are you up to it?

170
00:18:15,554 --> 00:18:17,263
The lemon drops are magical.

171
00:18:17,347 --> 00:18:20,764
When taking them,
you forget that it is difficult to breathe.

172
00:18:29,985 --> 00:18:31,694
Say a prayer.

173
00:18:36,867 --> 00:18:38,410
It works.

174
00:18:42,789 --> 00:18:45,246
Stick your head in. Isn't that good?

175
00:18:45,333 --> 00:18:47,208
Isn't it though?

176
00:18:47,794 --> 00:18:49,455
- Try it!
- Take Christy!

177
00:18:49,546 --> 00:18:52,667
Come on, stick your face in. Look at it.

178
00:18:54,301 --> 00:18:56,129
You're a genius, Dad.

179
00:19:03,393 --> 00:19:04,936
Hey, gringo!

180
00:19:05,020 --> 00:19:07,975
What's going on up there, whiting?

181
00:19:11,568 --> 00:19:14,440
<i>We got out as fast as we could.</i>

182
00:19:15,530 --> 00:19:18,698
<i>We went to the bank, took out our money...</i>

183
00:19:19,326 --> 00:19:22,778
<i>and went to the cinema, where it was deliciously cool.</i>

184
00:19:53,610 --> 00:19:56,731
Don't be sad. E.T. is in heaven.

185
00:19:57,280 --> 00:20:01,065
- They said he was going home.
- It's the same.

186
00:20:03,828 --> 00:20:05,158
No.

187
00:20:10,043 --> 00:20:11,586
I miss some things.

188
00:20:14,506 --> 00:20:16,215
What do you miss?

189
00:20:16,883 --> 00:20:20,384
Different things. I have no one to play with.

190
00:20:21,763 --> 00:20:26,225
- You can play with your sister.
- No. She plays with the video camera.

191
00:20:27,435 --> 00:20:30,188
I have no one to tell secrets to.

192
00:20:30,689 --> 00:20:33,263
Christy tells hers to the camera.

193
00:20:34,234 --> 00:20:37,106
And I don't get to hear what she says.

194
00:20:38,655 --> 00:20:41,361
And you're not playing with us anymore.

195
00:20:44,619 --> 00:20:48,239
- I'll play with you then.
- Not like before.

196
00:20:57,215 --> 00:20:58,675
Come on!

197
00:21:02,429 --> 00:21:05,550
Come on again.
Hit the balloon and you'll get a prize.

198
00:21:07,309 --> 00:21:09,516
- Take a number.
- Dad!

199
00:21:10,395 --> 00:21:13,598
Dad, you can win E.T.!

200
00:21:18,403 --> 00:21:22,781
It's a game of chance. Light as nothing.

201
00:21:22,866 --> 00:21:25,737
Just throw the ball through the hole
seven times...

202
00:21:25,827 --> 00:21:28,746
- then you win E.T.
- Seven times? No more?

203
00:21:29,748 --> 00:21:31,492
- Are adults allowed to play?
- Yes, then.

204
00:21:31,583 --> 00:21:33,458
- Light as nothing.
- That will be $2.

205
00:21:33,543 --> 00:21:35,952
You can roll as long as you double the amount.

206
00:21:36,046 --> 00:21:38,798
If you win,
you get a prize and your money back.

207
00:21:38,882 --> 00:21:43,296
- Do you get the money back if you win?
- Yes. And you can choose a doll.

208
00:21:47,891 --> 00:21:48,923
Yes!

209
00:21:49,017 --> 00:21:51,307
- There was one.
- Come on, Johnny.

210
00:21:56,149 --> 00:21:59,352
- You have two. Five left. $4.
- We can do this.

211
00:21:59,444 --> 00:22:01,936
Come on, Dad. You are so good.

212
00:22:02,030 --> 00:22:04,189
Take it easy. I'll make it happen.

213
00:22:04,282 --> 00:22:07,783
- Mom, is dad going to win?
- Of course, friend.

214
00:22:10,830 --> 00:22:12,492
Come on, Dad.

215
00:22:14,125 --> 00:22:15,502
Yes!

216
00:22:15,585 --> 00:22:18,255
Three, four, five. Very good. Only two left.

217
00:22:23,635 --> 00:22:25,178
$8.

218
00:22:28,056 --> 00:22:30,299
Gambling. Light as nothing.

219
00:22:30,392 --> 00:22:33,310
You can throw
as long as you double the amount.

220
00:22:33,395 --> 00:22:34,558
Dirt!

221
00:22:34,729 --> 00:22:38,182
- Number five, two to go. $16.
- We'll take the chance.

222
00:22:39,150 --> 00:22:43,897
- Come on, Dad. Just two more.
- Right. I can do it. Take it easy.

223
00:22:46,157 --> 00:22:50,156
$32. We have $32 over here.

224
00:22:50,328 --> 00:22:54,078
- I don't need an audience.
- You are the draw.

225
00:22:58,628 --> 00:23:01,381
Gambling. Light as nothing.

226
00:23:13,059 --> 00:23:15,978
$64. Are we done?

227
00:23:16,938 --> 00:23:19,015
Angela. Over here.

228
00:23:20,859 --> 00:23:22,484
I have 55.

229
00:23:22,569 --> 00:23:25,856
- Here, I have 5 more.
- Only need 4 more.

230
00:23:25,947 --> 00:23:29,150
- It doesn't matter, dad.
- No thanks.

231
00:23:29,284 --> 00:23:31,159
Just accept them, Johnny.

232
00:23:31,703 --> 00:23:35,073
$1 in change for the big girl.
Only one left.

233
00:23:35,165 --> 00:23:38,617
One ball left for the big doll
to the little girl.

234
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:42,128
Don't let him break
your concentration, Johnny.

235
00:23:52,557 --> 00:23:55,096
- Give me the rent.
- What?

236
00:23:56,478 --> 00:24:00,429
- Give me the rent.
- Don't do this to me tonight.

237
00:24:00,899 --> 00:24:04,067
I can't lose again in front of the kids, Sarah.

238
00:24:22,587 --> 00:24:25,375
Wait a minute. We have $128 here.

239
00:24:26,341 --> 00:24:27,753
Come on, Dad.

240
00:24:35,976 --> 00:24:39,559
- Now we are done.
- Leave them alone.

241
00:24:42,440 --> 00:24:44,185
Hello!

242
00:24:49,573 --> 00:24:51,815
We can't waste all the money.

243
00:24:52,868 --> 00:24:57,281
I believe in you, the children believe in you,
and you can win that doll.

244
00:24:57,664 --> 00:25:00,583
- Come on.
- You win. I know that.

245
00:25:12,179 --> 00:25:16,473
<i>Then I used all my willpower
to quiet the crowd.</i>

246
