I need morphine.

758
01:19:46,160 --> 01:19:47,821
Morphine, sister.

759
01:19:48,245 --> 01:19:50,737
Johnny, why isn't the baby crying?

760
01:19:50,831 --> 01:19:53,917
- Just go with the child.
- I'm going.

761
01:20:14,438 --> 01:20:16,811
We have stabilized her for now...

762
01:20:17,107 --> 01:20:20,940
but she must have a blood transfusion
within a couple of hours.

763
01:20:32,206 --> 01:20:33,582
Okay?

764
01:20:35,376 --> 01:20:39,955
Everything will be alright.
The child must have a blood transfusion.

765
01:20:41,840 --> 01:20:45,886
We have to sign
on a consent form. Both of them.

766
01:20:47,680 --> 01:20:49,175
Is that okay?

767
01:20:57,064 --> 01:21:00,897
All blood is bad.
Mateo said all blood is bad.

768
01:21:01,735 --> 01:21:04,358
You don't give my child bad blood.

769
01:21:06,865 --> 01:21:09,025
You gave my child bad blood.

770
01:21:10,411 --> 01:21:14,244
That's why he died.
That's why he fell down the stairs.

771
01:21:16,750 --> 01:21:18,993
This is the new baby.

772
01:21:24,842 --> 01:21:28,342
He tried to climb over the gate.
And then he fell.

773
01:21:30,347 --> 01:21:32,258
Why did you set it up?

774
01:21:36,312 --> 01:21:38,056
- Where is he?
- Who?

775
01:21:38,188 --> 01:21:39,470
Frankie.

776
01:21:41,775 --> 01:21:44,065
Frankie has passed away, Sarah.

777
01:21:57,833 --> 01:22:00,456
You should have taken the gate down.

778
01:22:02,087 --> 01:22:06,003
It's your fault.
You should have taken the gate down!

779
01:22:06,675 --> 01:22:08,752
- You are hiding him.
- No.

780
01:22:09,595 --> 01:22:13,131
- I want Frankie. I want my child!
- Calm down.

781
01:22:14,016 --> 01:22:18,097
- Where is he? I want Frankie.
- Calm down. Take it easy. Doctor!

782
01:22:18,520 --> 01:22:21,143
It's your fault he fell down the stairs.

783
01:22:21,232 --> 01:22:23,439
Can you press the call button?

784
01:22:23,525 --> 01:22:26,397
Why didn't you take down the gate?

785
01:22:26,487 --> 01:22:28,315
- It's going well.
- No.

786
01:22:28,405 --> 01:22:31,028
I'm begging you. Johnny. Please be kind.

787
01:22:31,116 --> 01:22:34,451
No, please. I want to see my child.

788
01:22:34,870 --> 01:22:37,493
- Don't take the new child.
- I'm not taking her.

789
01:22:37,581 --> 01:22:40,784
- Save my child, Johnny.
- I promise.

790
01:22:48,634 --> 01:22:49,880
Yes.

791
01:22:53,347 --> 01:22:56,219
If the child dies, don't wake me.

792
01:23:03,023 --> 01:23:06,191
- There is only one other solution.
- What then?

793
01:23:07,111 --> 01:23:09,567
- Do you have 0 rhesus minus?
- I have.

794
01:23:11,824 --> 01:23:13,699
Christy has 0 rhesus minus.

795
01:23:16,412 --> 01:23:19,414
- What if I have it?
- Got what?

796
01:23:21,584 --> 01:23:23,245
Mateo's disease.

797
01:23:26,297 --> 01:23:28,586
It's not possible, Christy.

798
01:23:29,633 --> 01:23:31,508
How do you know that?

799
01:23:31,969 --> 01:23:34,128
God will not let that happen.

800
01:23:35,222 --> 01:23:37,299
You don't believe in God.

801
01:23:39,393 --> 01:23:42,478
- I'm scared.
- Don't be afraid.

802
01:23:43,022 --> 01:23:44,731
Everyone dies.

803
01:23:52,364 --> 01:23:55,817
- Will she survive it?
- She can't survive without it.

804
01:23:59,079 --> 01:24:02,247
That's what the doctors said before they opened Frankie up, too.

805
01:24:03,209 --> 01:24:07,254
- What are we doing?
- I give her blood.

806
01:24:08,881 --> 01:24:10,673
Is it a decision?

807
01:24:12,343 --> 01:24:14,420
Christy gives her blood.

808
01:24:22,978 --> 01:24:25,102
Are you okay, my girl?

809
01:24:28,025 --> 01:24:30,019
Don't come here with "my girl".

810
01:24:30,736 --> 01:24:34,071
I have carried this family
on my shoulders for over a year.

811
01:24:34,657 --> 01:24:36,697
Ever since Frankie died.

812
01:24:38,285 --> 01:24:40,279
He was my brother too.

813
01:24:41,455 --> 01:24:45,370
It's not my fault he's dead.
It is not my fault that I am alive.

814
01:24:45,459 --> 01:24:46,741
Christie.

815
01:24:49,213 --> 01:24:51,882
Mom cried constantly
because he was her son.

816
01:24:52,800 --> 01:24:57,795
But he was my brother too.
I cried too, when no one was watching.

817
01:24:59,765 --> 01:25:03,016
- And I talked to him every night.
- She did it.

818
01:25:07,648 --> 01:25:11,978
- I talked to him every night until...
- Until what?

819
01:25:16,490 --> 01:25:19,492
Until I realized it was me
I talked to.

820
01:25:27,126 --> 01:25:28,918
I'm taking her home.

821
01:25:29,003 --> 01:25:31,542
- Fine. Thank you.
- No reason.

822
01:25:33,507 --> 01:25:35,548
There was no coverage on the check.

823
01:25:42,975 --> 01:25:47,270
<i>I sat there with dad,
and all the sounds of New York disappeared.</i>

824
01:25:49,982 --> 01:25:52,900
<i>All I heard,
was the blood pounding in my ear.</i>

825
01:25:54,445 --> 01:25:56,604
<i>But I felt happy.</i>

826
01:25:58,532 --> 01:26:03,029
<i>I was wondering about Frankie
had felt like this: like something special.</i>

827
01:26:04,997 --> 01:26:08,449
<i>Everyone looks at you as if in a mirror.</i>

828
01:26:08,918 --> 01:26:12,038
<i>And smiles. Just not with the eyes.</i>

829
01:26:16,800 --> 01:26:19,174
<i>Did Frankie know he was going to die?</i>

830
01:26:20,262 --> 01:26:23,217
<i>Was that why
he always nodded and smiled at us?</i>

831
01:26:49,875 --> 01:26:52,035
When he died, I cursed God.

832
01:26:53,462 --> 01:26:56,168
I said, "You'll never see these tears...

833
01:26:56,257 --> 01:26:58,879
"run down my cheek again."

834
01:27:01,136 --> 01:27:02,964
So now I can't cry.

835
01:27:09,311 --> 01:27:12,099
I thought I'd pop in here…

836
01:27:13,899 --> 01:27:17,186
and then you would wake up
and hold my hand.

837
01:27:19,572 --> 01:27:22,906
I was going to cry,
and then the child would be fine.

838
01:27:24,243 --> 01:27:26,320
Everything was going to be alright.

839
01:27:34,044 --> 01:27:36,121
We need a miracle, Mateo.

840
01:27:38,716 --> 01:27:40,840
Hello, ire. Stop.

841
01:27:46,307 --> 01:27:48,134
Can't you say hello?

842
01:27:48,934 --> 01:27:51,426
What is it? What's the matter?

843
01:27:52,771 --> 01:27:56,355
- Sorry.
- Bad day?

844
01:27:57,192 --> 01:28:00,563
- You can say that.
- The whole world has had a bad day.

845
01:28:03,365 --> 01:28:06,320
Can't I get a pair of buckles?

846
01:28:08,287 --> 01:28:10,993
- Come on.
- I have no money to give you.

847
01:28:11,999 --> 01:28:15,451
Excuse me. How stupid I am.
I shouldn't bother you.

848
01:28:16,670 --> 01:28:19,506
Look a little brighter at life.
Better times are coming.

849
01:28:21,383 --> 01:28:25,678
Come on, you Irish brawler.
Now I'm coming to get you.

850
01:28:27,556 --> 01:28:29,466
Just give me some money.

851
01:28:29,558 --> 01:28:32,181
Not because of me. They are for Angela.

852
01:28:32,478 --> 01:28:35,231
Put your hand in your pocket.

853
01:28:35,564 --> 01:28:38,732
- Relax.
- The other pocket.

854
01:28:40,402 --> 01:28:43,986
The other pocket. Faster, anger. Let me see.

855
01:28:45,115 --> 01:28:46,527
Out with it.

856
01:28:47,243 --> 01:28:49,569
- I don't know what it is.
- Take it out.

857
01:28:49,662 --> 01:28:53,079
I'll take it out. Here, please.

858
01:29:01,423 --> 01:29:03,084
I just needed money.

859
01:29:03,926 --> 01:29:05,386
I'm sorry for that.

860
01:29:06,720 --> 01:29:08,548
That's enough.

861
01:29:15,563 --> 01:29:19,857
End. Excuse me. I'm sorry for that.

862
01:29:26,532 --> 01:29:30,744
- Are we still friends?
- Move and travel.

863
01:29:34,498 --> 01:29:38,117
<i>We sat and waited
that the baby should give us a sign of life.</i>

864
01:29:39,253 --> 01:29:41,792
<i>She just lay there and lay there.</i>

865
01:31:55,514 --> 01:31:59,133
<i>The hospital bill came. It was on:</i>

866
01:31:59,435 --> 01:32:03,647
<i>$30,420.20.</i>

867
01:32:04,064 --> 01:32:06,853
Just let me in for the audition.

868
01:32:07,359 --> 01:32:09,104
I give them what they want.

869
01:32:09,194 --> 01:32:11,235
The bill is ready.

870
01:32:12,239 --> 01:32:13,616
Right.

871
01:32:18,329 --> 01:32:20,536
- The bill has been paid.
- What do you mean?

872
01:32:22,750 --> 01:32:25,787
It is paid for by a Mateo Kuamey.

873
01:32:28,297 --> 01:32:30,089
You owe nothing.

874
01:32:33,969 --> 01:32:37,968
<i>Look, look my playmate
Come back</i>

875
01:32:38,057 --> 01:32:40,513
<i>Finally, dad got a role.</i>

876
01:32:40,726 --> 01:32:43,052
<i>And then he brought good news.</i>

877
01:32:43,145 --> 01:32:44,973
<i>Since 1982</i>

878
01:32:45,064 --> 01:32:46,689
I have good news.

879
01:32:46,774 --> 01:32:49,895
Sarah Mateo Sullivan
comes home from the hospital.

880
01:32:52,947 --> 01:32:54,358
Yes, cool!

881
01:32:58,619 --> 01:33:01,158
- Look who it is.
- Hello to you.

882
01:33:01,330 --> 01:33:03,039
- Do you want to see?
- Yes.

883
01:33:03,582 --> 01:33:05,872
- May I be allowed, mom?
- Yes, fine.

884
01:33:12,967 --> 01:33:14,545
Alright, see you.

885
01:33:15,636 --> 01:33:17,297
Big yawn.

886
01:33:39,326 --> 01:33:40,822
What's the matter?

887
01:33:41,787 --> 01:33:44,077
- He didn't get to say goodbye.
- What?

888
01:33:44,707 --> 01:33:46,617
He didn't get to say goodbye.

889
01:33:52,548 --> 01:33:54,542
It was a girl!

890
01:34:42,389 --> 01:34:44,134
The baby is sleeping.

891
01:34:48,896 --> 01:34:50,177
Christie.

892
01:34:56,695 --> 01:34:58,356
Come here.

893
01:35:03,160 --> 01:35:05,948
Look up there and tell me what you see.

894
01:35:06,914 --> 01:35:07,994
Full moon.

895
01:35:08,082 --> 01:35:10,159
What else do you see?

896
01:35:11,877 --> 01:35:13,076
Stars.

897
01:35:13,546 --> 01:35:15,456
Don't you see Mateo?

898
01:35:17,800 --> 01:35:20,506
He rides past the moon.

899
01:35:21,387 --> 01:35:24,093
I think he's waving goodbye to Ariel.

900
01:35:24,682 --> 01:35:26,391
- Shall we say it?
- Yes.

901
01:35:38,362 --> 01:35:40,106
Look up there.

902
01:35:40,197 --> 01:35:42,772
It's Mateo riding past the moon.

903
01:35:42,866 --> 01:35:44,528
- Where?
- There. See.

904
01:35:44,618 --> 01:35:47,406
- Don't you see that he is waving at you?
- No.

905
01:35:48,581 --> 01:35:52,911
- He's right there.
- He's there, he's riding past the moon.

906
01:35:54,503 --> 01:35:56,296
- Do you see him?
- No.

907
01:35:56,380 --> 01:35:59,501
Don't you see him waving at you?
He waves goodbye.

908
01:35:59,592 --> 01:36:01,502
Just as he promised.

909
01:36:01,844 --> 01:36:03,884
Yes of course. Have at it, Mateo.

910
01:36:03,971 --> 01:36:07,388
- Have at it, Mateo.
- Have at it, Mateo.

911
01:36:08,100 --> 01:36:11,055
Have at it, Mateo. Take care of Frankie.

912
01:36:12,438 --> 01:36:15,012
- Take care of Frankie.
- Watch out...

913
01:36:20,738 --> 01:36:23,312
<i>And then I asked for the third wish.</i>

914
01:36:25,701 --> 01:36:27,944
Say goodbye to Frankie, Dad.

915
01:36:30,039 --> 01:36:31,202
What?

916
01:36:32,708 --> 01:36:34,702
Say goodbye to Frankie.

917
01:36:41,383 --> 01:36:45,382
- Goodbye, Frankie.
- He can't hear you, Dad.

918
01:36:54,271 --> 01:36:55,980
Bye, Frankie.

919
01:37:13,374 --> 01:37:15,035
Go your way.

920
01:37:26,679 --> 01:37:28,090
Daddy needs you.

921
01:37:56,917 --> 01:38:00,833
<i>It was equally difficult for Frankie to smile
with a malignant tumor...</i>

922
01:38:02,298 --> 01:38:04,837
<i>like for dad to cry afterwards.</i>

923
01:38:05,676 --> 01:38:07,753
<i>But both managed it.</i>

924
01:38:10,806 --> 01:38:13,298
<i>I'm turning this off now.</i>

925
01:38:14,476 --> 01:38:17,313
<i>That's not how I want to see Frankie anymore.</i>

926
01:38:31,160 --> 01:38:33,913
<i>Do you still have a picture of me in your head?</i>

927
01:38:35,247 --> 01:38:38,415
<i>That's the kind of picture I want of Frankie.</i>

928
01:38:39,752 --> 01:38:42,623
<i>Something you can always have in your head.</i>

929
01:38:45,216 --> 01:38:47,790
<i>So when you go back to reality...</i>

930
01:38:49,511 --> 01:38:51,304
<i>want to ask Frankie...</i>

931
01:38:52,973 --> 01:38:56,972
<i>about being so kind as to let me go.</i>

932
01:39:09,531 --> 01:39:13,364
this film is appropriated
Frankie Sheridan's memory
